Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.23,0:00:12.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If ever there were a devilish act \Ncommitted in this world,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.34,0:00:14.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,this incident would \Ndefinitely have to be it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.02,0:00:16.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The devil, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.13,0:00:21.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We State Alchemists are human weapons in the service of the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.00,0:00:23.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Whenever something comes up, \Nwe are called upon,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.30,0:00:25.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and if ordered to, \Nwe must dirty our own hands.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.38,0:00:28.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,From the point of doing this \Nor that with other people's lives,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.91,0:00:32.65,Dialogue,,20,20,0,,there's not a huge difference between the position we're in and the actions that Tucker took.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.47,0:00:36.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is the reasoning of an adult.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.70,0:00:39.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But those children are still so...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.73,0:00:45.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother... Brother, the Lt. Colonel...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.98,0:00:49.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's a wasted effort.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.05,0:00:55.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It is not possible to reconstruct \Na living creature once its life has been lost.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.29,0:00:57.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not for any alchemist.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.13,0:01:01.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who is it going to please to bring an abortive Chimera back to life?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.70,0:01:05.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There will be even greater suffering and anguish than this
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.05,0:01:07.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,waiting for you further down the road you have chosen.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.15,0:01:11.11,Dialogue,,20,20,0,,As such, you must keep moving forward, \Neven if you have to force yourselves to accept this.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.11,0:01:12.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Accept this, you say?!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.90,0:01:17.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There is some purpose you're trying to accomplish, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.46,0:01:19.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you have time \Nto just stand still?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.98,0:01:24.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For crying out loud,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.24,0:01:27.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I won't even be able to get in \Na good bath with my daughter.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.64,0:01:28.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Here?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.33,0:01:29.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.00,0:01:32.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,From here on, this is a job for \Nthe Investigations Department.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.20,0:01:33.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stand aside.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.28,0:01:41.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is something awful.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.96,0:01:45.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is this the work of that serial killer?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.10,0:01:47.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That guy specializes in young ladies, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.44,0:01:49.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's more, this one \Nhasn't been carved up.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.64,0:01:52.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's almost as if...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.03,0:01:56.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,they were blown up from the inside or something, from the look of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.70,0:02:03.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Man cannot obtain anything \Nwithout first sacrificing something.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.44,0:02:08.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In order to obtain anything, \Nsomething of equal value is required.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.73,0:02:13.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is alchemy's \NLaw of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.47,0:02:19.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the time, we believed that \Nto be the true way of the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.06,0:04:15.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's a pretty serious look on your face.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.04,0:04:17.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For some reason, it feels like I'm at my wit's end.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.28,0:04:21.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And here I thought I was through wavering all over the place.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.28,0:04:24.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So then,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.93,0:04:26.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,what are these orders?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.48,0:04:29.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.02,0:04:37.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sort out the materials here and organize them,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.21,0:04:40.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and make yourself completely familiar with the results of Tucker's research.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.97,0:04:44.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you telling me to \Ntake over Tucker's research?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.68,0:04:46.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He went about it the wrong way,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.93,0:04:49.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but there were portions of Tucker's research that have merit for the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.11,0:04:52.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then you can let Tucker \Ntake care of it, can't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.08,0:04:53.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.62,0:04:55.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.76,0:04:59.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Apparently, his guilt was obvious,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.94,0:05:03.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so at the discretion of the higher-ups, he was executed.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.57,0:05:08.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You mean this was covered up! \NHow could they?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.02,0:05:11.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Pledge your loyalty to the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.39,0:05:14.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's the main principle \Ngoverning State Alchemists.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.91,0:05:26.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Say, it looks like Tucker-san was also doing research on the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.68,0:05:29.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh? That's nice.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.11,0:05:33.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How long are you going to sulk like this, Brother?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.93,0:05:38.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Philosopher's Stone is the ultimate secret to us alchemists, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.36,0:05:40.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It increases your faculty without bound
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.34,0:05:43.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and makes transmutation \Nbeyond principles possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.19,0:05:46.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In other words, the things that \Nwe weren't able to do could be—
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.05,0:05:48.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That thing is just a legend!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.73,0:05:50.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's a fairy tale!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.84,0:05:54.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But if Tucker-san, a State Alchemist, was doing research on it, then...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.91,0:05:56.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who gives a damn \Nabout his research?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.27,0:06:00.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al, have you forgotten about Nina?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.39,0:06:08.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I cannot permit it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.82,0:06:10.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why not?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.26,0:06:13.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That serial killer might've done Nina in like that, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.80,0:06:15.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll help out in finding him!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.86,0:06:18.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And the work you were ordered to do?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.01,0:06:20.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What about analyzing Tucker's research?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.68,0:06:23.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't want to.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.62,0:06:25.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll investigate on my own, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.53,0:06:27.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay. In that case,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.64,0:06:29.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,leave that here.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.88,0:06:32.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I intended to.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.68,0:06:36.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.75,0:06:40.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just a minute!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.64,0:06:42.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're not the only one
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.29,0:06:44.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,who's upset over not being able to do anything for Nina, Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.99,0:06:47.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're alchemists, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.01,0:06:50.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Catching criminals isn't \Nsomething that we can do.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.26,0:06:54.03,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,We do research so that if another girl like Nina \Never comes along who we can save...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.57,0:07:09.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.39,0:07:11.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You... You're the guy from the library.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.98,0:07:19.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you were able to come \Nand go at the first branch,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.04,0:07:21.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,does that mean you're \Na State Alchemist?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.37,0:07:25.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the time, yeah. \NBut not anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.28,0:07:26.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is that so?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.68,0:07:28.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're better off.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.68,0:07:34.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You're better off, that is...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.20,0:07:38.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}assuming you don't want to be destroyed by this arm.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.69,0:07:48.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed and Al sure will be surprised!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.36,0:07:51.83,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,They'd never expect me, Winry-chan, \Nto come all this way and congratulate them!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.60,0:07:53.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All righty!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.00,0:07:58.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Excuse me, Lt. Hawkeye?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.20,0:07:59.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.54,0:08:02.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But then, I don't know much about the Philosopher's Stone, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.34,0:08:06.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At least, I've never heard of it actually existing.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.91,0:08:09.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I thought it was just a legend.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.04,0:08:10.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I see...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.36,0:08:15.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, I think you'd be better off \Nnot paying any interest in such a thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.90,0:08:21.50,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,It's said that bad things happen to anyone that gets close to the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.50,0:08:25.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, you're interested in the \NPhilosopher's Stone, are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.34,0:08:29.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who is this?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.10,0:08:30.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Th-This gentleman is...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.93,0:08:35.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You want to obtain the\NPhilosopher's Stone, do you?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.77,0:08:36.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.41,0:08:38.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For what reason?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.01,0:08:41.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For human—
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.15,0:08:45.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I mean, I want to recover \Nsomething that my brother has lost.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.40,0:08:49.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh? You must think highly of your brother, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.16,0:08:53.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't know any particulars myself,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.51,0:08:56.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but there are a lot of people who \Nbelieve in the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.51,0:08:59.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's more, once in a while, \NI hear stories about alchemists
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.67,0:09:02.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,who have succeeded in creating a Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.42,0:09:05.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Such rumors naturally have a way of gathering around the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.11,0:09:10.94,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,There should be a number of records about it \Nin the first branch of the Central Library.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.94,0:09:12.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Really?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.88,0:09:17.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But then, only State Alchemists are allowed to make use of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.65,0:09:23.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, a State Alchemist could verify \Nwhether the rumors are true or not.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.81,0:09:34.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Führer, why would you listen in \Non something like that?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.73,0:09:38.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's good for the youth \Nto pursue their dreams.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.70,0:09:42.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't you think so, Lieutenant?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.40,0:09:43.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sure...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.98,0:09:50.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,See, I'm right! You think \Nshe's cute too, don't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.85,0:09:52.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Y-Yeah, I guess...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.88,0:10:00.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What do you think?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.49,0:10:04.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You think she takes after me?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.24,0:10:07.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What can I say? Everyone says so!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.15,0:10:10.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't bother me, Pops!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.45,0:10:12.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's no need for that kind of talk.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.82,0:10:16.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not when I've been showing you the classified analysis of the serial killer.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.17,0:10:20.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You owe me two. One for the train, and one for your wife's delivery.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.30,0:10:25.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, yeah? Well, in any case, we're at a standstill.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.36,0:10:28.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The crimes happen within the city, but there are no witnesses.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.37,0:10:30.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The bodies are outright sliced up,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.28,0:10:33.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but nobody believes that he could do it all in such a short time.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.80,0:10:37.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Could he have killed them \Nand then brought the bodies around?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.13,0:10:39.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How much time has passed from the time of death?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.76,0:10:42.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Not even the investigators \Nare clear on that very often.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.98,0:10:44.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But between the military and police,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.42,0:10:46.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,we've opened up and checked the trunk of every car...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.34,0:10:50.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,coming into the city.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.02,0:10:53.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There must be some sort of blind spot.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.80,0:10:55.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A car that can hide the bodies, \Nor something...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.71,0:10:58.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Or maybe it's the work of an alchemist...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.02,0:11:01.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Alchemists are not murderers!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.22,0:11:08.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Uh, are you Edward Elric-san?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.93,0:11:10.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.28,0:11:13.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's a visitor to see you at the Headquarters reception desk.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.30,0:11:14.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A visitor?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.04,0:11:19.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Howdy!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.87,0:11:21.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thanks, as usual!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.83,0:11:22.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.80,0:11:26.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They held the state \Ncertification exams again, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.37,0:11:27.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Y-Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.76,0:11:29.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, did you hear?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.17,0:11:32.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This time, there was a twelve-year-old who passed the test.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.85,0:11:35.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I hear he just does this with his hands,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.23,0:11:37.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and just like that, he can transmute.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.22,0:11:39.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Really?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.00,0:11:41.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There, the blond one.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.00,0:11:43.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And he's just a child, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.28,0:11:47.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, come to think of it, \Nwatch out for that one guy.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.28,0:11:51.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They say he only \Ncuts up the pretty ones.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.09,0:11:53.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh my, are you worried about me?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.94,0:11:55.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.21,0:11:57.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I sure hope they catch him soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.22,0:11:58.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You bet.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.82,0:12:00.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, about these incidents...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.23,0:12:03.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Have you heard anything else?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.95,0:12:09.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How long is Ed going to \Nkeep me waiting?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.67,0:12:20.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's a refrigeration unit!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.35,0:12:26.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Central sure does have \Nthe latest cars. How nice!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.05,0:12:28.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I sure would like to dismantle it!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.43,0:12:31.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid having it dismantled would put me out.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.18,0:12:34.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry! Is this your truck?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.98,0:12:38.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's right. This is my \Nfood shop's delivery truck.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.76,0:12:46.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is something the matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.03,0:12:47.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you'd like, would you \Ncare to look inside?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.96,0:12:51.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? I can?! Thanks so much!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.65,0:12:58.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.98,0:13:01.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I told her to wait right here.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.65,0:13:03.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's strange...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.25,0:13:05.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Elric-san?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.06,0:13:15.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is this...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.60,0:13:21.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Winry?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.58,0:13:22.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.68,0:13:28.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Was there a car stopped here?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.15,0:13:31.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, there are always \Nrefrigerated trucks stopping here,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.12,0:13:33.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,whose dealers serve \Nthe military's cafeteria.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.14,0:13:35.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Refrigerated truck?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.04,0:13:37.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Something that could hide a body?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.85,0:13:39.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It couldn't be...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.00,0:13:41.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Elric-san?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.04,0:14:04.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, are you all right?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.41,0:14:08.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Were you kidnapped as well?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.94,0:14:10.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Over there, there's someone else.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.28,0:14:15.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There is? Okay, let's take them and get out of here, quick!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.62,0:14:17.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll be here with you, \Nso don't worry—
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.84,0:14:33.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Good morning, junior.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.33,0:14:34.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why, you!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.48,0:14:41.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I heard that you can transmute \Nwithout using transmutation circles,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.28,0:14:43.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so just to be safe...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.94,0:14:49.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let me introduce myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.28,0:14:51.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm the shop's owner, Barry.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.95,0:14:53.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A man?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.66,0:14:58.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As a reward for making it this far, \Nlet me show you something you'll like.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.50,0:15:08.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Winry!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.70,0:15:13.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm about to craftily dissect this little girl.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.16,0:15:14.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Be sure to watch closely, now,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.96,0:15:16.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mr. State Alchemist.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.20,0:15:19.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop! Why are you doing this?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.24,0:15:21.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.74,0:15:25.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well now, because I enjoy it, I suppose.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.77,0:15:30.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The first person I killed was my wife.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.60,0:15:33.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We were having some \Npetty argument, you see.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.42,0:15:35.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then, without meaning to, I killed her.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.62,0:15:39.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But then, she cut up so neatly, you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.80,0:15:44.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,After that, I started wanting to \Ncut people up even more neatly.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.74,0:15:47.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I wanted everyone to see.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.34,0:15:50.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How can one person kill another for something like that?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.42,0:15:52.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, but they can!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.30,0:15:56.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Given just the slightest opportunity, a person can kill another.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.27,0:15:56.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stay back!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.38,0:16:02.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If they go off to war, it's even easier for one person to kill another.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.42,0:16:04.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why do you suppose that is?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.00,0:16:05.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I-I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.70,0:16:11.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's because people \N{\i1}want{\i0} to kill each other.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.42,0:16:14.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,On the battlefield, I saw \Na State Alchemist just like you
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.52,0:16:17.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,kill other people with ease.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.35,0:16:19.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Splat! Just like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.40,0:16:20.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.80,0:16:25.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.99,0:16:33.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why, you!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.05,0:16:43.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.40,0:17:04.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dammit!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.35,0:17:55.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.70,0:18:02.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It'll take more than that to kill me.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.82,0:18:06.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They're in here!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.92,0:18:08.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't move!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.45,0:18:11.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.96,0:18:13.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.48,0:18:15.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Does that hurt?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.46,0:18:18.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I thought I was going to get killed.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.38,0:18:22.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I really thought that I might die...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.56,0:18:24.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I was terrified...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.08,0:18:27.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Terribly scared...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.32,0:18:35.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thanks to Hughes-san realizing
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.72,0:18:41.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that trucks from this same food shop had passed inspections many times,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.52,0:18:44.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,we somehow managed to get there in time.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.06,0:18:50.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Afterward, the case of \NBarry the Chopper became famous,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.20,0:18:54.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and it would be spoken of as Brother's first distinguished achievement.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.85,0:18:59.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.00,0:19:04.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Philosopher's Stone \Nmight really exist.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.72,0:19:10.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But in order to search for it, you have to be certified as a State Alchemist.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.40,0:19:13.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Since I don't have a body,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.40,0:19:17.05,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,I can't really feel the terror you felt, \Nthinking you were going to be killed, Brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.80,0:19:19.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sure it must've been lonely...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.35,0:19:21.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and painful...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.10,0:19:26.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sure, I want my old body back...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.32,0:19:27.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,to be human again.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.97,0:19:29.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Once we find the \NPhilosopher's Stone,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.35,0:19:33.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,even if it means having to go against the flow of the rest of the world,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.08,0:19:35.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,as though nothing will ever come of it...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.06,0:19:39.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Having nearly been killed, I realized something...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.94,0:19:43.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All I could do was scream.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.12,0:19:46.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My mind just went completely blank.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.09,0:19:52.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I couldn't even bring myself to think there would be anyone to save me.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.39,0:19:55.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For all that we're able to do,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.50,0:19:59.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,we'll have our hands full just trying to get our own bodies back.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.21,0:20:00.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,To that end,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.64,0:20:04.49,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,whether it means being a dog of the military, or cursed as the devil, I don't care...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.95,0:20:07.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But then,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.48,0:20:12.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,we really aren't devils, much less gods.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.98,0:20:14.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're only human!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.08,0:20:21.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Tiny, insignificant humans, \Nwho couldn't even save Nina...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.68,0:20:28.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A condition, you say?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.45,0:20:30.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I will obey my duties to the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.62,0:20:34.92,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,As such, I would like to be told all information there is about the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.23,0:20:40.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When I have no other duties, permit me to search for the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.66,0:20:44.74,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Are you sure you want it to get out that you committed the sin of human transmutation?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:44.74,0:20:47.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Your brother will be \Nbrought into the laboratory
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.05,0:20:49.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,as an extraordinary \Nexample of transmutation.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.85,0:20:54.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At least, that's the way I {\i1}could{\i0} \Npressure you to make sure you stay in line.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.88,0:20:58.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay, very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.80,0:21:04.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But you will report to me everything you find out about the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.71,0:21:09.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You have been given \Na title from the Führer.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.05,0:21:12.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's quite an ironic title, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.10,0:21:21.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"We give the name 'Fullmetal' to thee,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.28,0:21:26.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Edward Elric, in the name of Führer King Bradley."
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.45,0:21:29.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Fullmetal?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:30.02,0:21:34.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,State Alchemists are given a silver watch, \Nas well as a second name.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.85,0:21:37.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The second name that you will bear is "Fullmetal."
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.50,0:21:40.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Fullmetal Alchemist.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.62,0:21:48.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I like it. It has an oppressive feel to it. \NSure, I'll take on that name!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.66,0:21:54.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,To celebrate, you're going to treat me \Nto all kinds of delicious things!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.00,0:21:55.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've got it backwards, don't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.83,0:21:58.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I fixed your arm, didn't I?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.05,0:22:08.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, I heard that the serial killer \Ndidn't have anything to do with Nina.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:08.20,0:22:11.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, he seems to have an alibi for that night.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:12.26,0:22:16.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then, I wonder who it was that wiped out Nina like that...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.87,0:23:40.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 3,0:23:40.52,0:23:44.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 9: "The Dog of the Military's \NSilver Watch"
Dialogue: 0,0:23:45.06,0:23:48.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I knew what it would mean to become a State Alchemist
Dialogue: 0,0:23:48.57,0:23:50.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,from the very beginning,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:51.47,0:23:52.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al...
